# Cyrillic / `_Pen_No__N` purge procedure

Every Tbilisi DWG that came through Russian / Soviet-era offices carries
layer names like
`New_2D Drafting - General_Pen_No__30_Pen_No__9_Pen_No__9_Pen_No__7`
and MText with `\fArial|c204` overrides (CP-1251 codepage). This rule
defines how to migrate them to the project standard from
`02-units-dims.mdc` and `00-georgian-text.mdc`.

## Step 0 — Triage

```
(setq old-count (length (vla-get-layers (vla-get-activedocument (vlax-get-acad-object)))))
```

If `old-count > 60` the file is almost certainly a legacy import.

## Step 1 — Layer-name → standard mapping

| Old layer pattern | New standard layer |
|---|---|
| `*Wall*`, `*Bearing*`, `*shenobeb*` | `WALL` |
| `*partition*`, `*tixar*` | `WALL-INNER` |
| `*Door*`, `*kar-*`, but **only door geometry** | `DOOR` |
| `*panjar*`, `*window*`, `*kar-panjara*` | `WINDOW` |
| `*Furniture*`, `*Interior*`, `*aveji*` | `FURN` |
| `*WC*`, `*lavabo*`, `*shower*`, `*bidet*`, `*plumbing*` | `FIX` |
| `*grid*`, `*axis*`, `*Reg_Nak*` | `GRID` |
| `*axis-label*`, `*bubble*` | `AXIS-LABEL` |
| `*zoma*`, `*dim*`, `*cota*` | `DIM` |
| `*text*`, `*anno*`, `*annotation*` | `TEXT` |
| `*title*`, `*werwera*`, `*frame*` | `TITLE` |
| `*topo*`, `*GAZI*`, `*sxivebi*`, `*momijnave*` | leave on the topo layer (xref residue) |
| `*ნაკვეთ*`, `*sakutreb*` | `PARCEL` (extra) |

> When in doubt, keep the entity on its current layer and inspect by hand.

## Step 2 — Run the remap

`scripts/utilities/layer-remap-to-standard.lsp` does this:

1. Builds the mapping table.
2. For each entity in modelspace it inspects the current layer name,
   matches against the rules above and re-assigns layer.
3. Writes a per-rule counter to `layer-remap-report.txt`.

## Step 3 — Purge unused layers

```
(command "_.PURGE" "_LA" "*" "_N")
(command "_.PURGE" "_BL" "*" "_N")
(command "_.PURGE" "_R" "_BL" "*" "_N")
```

## Step 4 — Migrate MText fonts

Search every `MText` for `\fArial|c204` and replace with `\fSylfaen|b0|i0;`.

Pseudocode:

```
(setq ss (ssget "_X" '((0 . "MTEXT"))))
(repeat (sslength ss)
  (setq e (ssname ss 0))
  (setq ed (entget e))
  (setq new (vl-string-subst "\\fSylfaen|b0|i0;"
                             "\\fArial|b0|i0|c204|p0;"
                             (cdr (assoc 1 ed))))
  (entmod (subst (cons 1 new) (assoc 1 ed) ed))
  (setq ss (ssdel e ss)))
```

## Step 5 — Recreate the standard text style

```
(command "_.-STYLE" "GEO" "Sylfaen.ttf" "0" "1" "0" "N" "N" "N")
(command "_.STYLE" "Standard" "" "" "" "" "" "")  ; reset Standard
```

## Step 6 — Validate

After remap run:

```
(load "C:/Users/PCZONE.GE/autocad-mcp/scripts/validators/check-title-block.lsp")
(load "C:/Users/PCZONE.GE/autocad-mcp/scripts/validators/check-min-rooms.lsp")
```

and also the MCP `validate_drawing` + `compute_metrics`.

## Common pitfalls

- **Don't lose the `New_ნაკვეთების კონტურები გრგ2_*` layer** — it's the
  parcel boundary from GRG-2 and you'll need it for K-coefficient
  calculation. Keep it on its own layer or remap to `PARCEL`.
- **Don't merge `kar-panjara` doors and windows blindly.** That layer
  often holds **both**. Use entity bounding-box analysis to split:
  short ones (< 1 200 mm) → `DOOR`, longer ones → `WINDOW`.
- **HATCH on the `G-Anno-Nplt_Pen_No__151` layer is the cyan label
  highlight under area numbers** — keep on a separate `TEXT-HILITE` if
  the office uses it.
- **MTEXT with no Georgian content** (just numbers like `8.0 m²`) —
  leave the font alone; only force Sylfaen on actual Georgian text.
- **Annotative scale entities** can break after layer rename. Run
  `_REGENALL` to re-cache.
